],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Testing: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py tests/unit/test_review_bot_finding_publish.py` — omits tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py","Plan voter.py delta: 'Partition, then post with comments='","tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py:180 `def post_vote(self, change_id, revision, value, message, robot_comments=None):` — no `comments` param, and this `_FakeGerrit` (defined at :162, used on the non-merge PASS path) defines no `get_revision_files`"],"finding":"The `post_vote` signature change (new `comments` param) and the modified voter.py:700 call site passing `comments=` omit a duck-typed test double: `tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py:180` defines `_FakeGerrit.post_vote(self, change_id, revision, value, message, robot_comments=None)` and lacks `get_revision_files`. This fake is exercised on the non-merge PASS path the plan edits, yet the plan's test inventory names only `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` and the new `test_review_bot_finding_publish.py`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f99022533d6e91f7e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Testing' section (test file list) and 'voter.py (minimal delta at the post_vote call site, line 700)' — inventory for `post_vote` / `get_revision_files`","norm_id":"n095723af18211016","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py: the voter passes `comments=` to `_FakeGerrit.post_vote`, which rejects the keyword -> TypeError, breaking the PASS-path token-usage integration test the plan does not run","tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py `_FakeGerrit`: new `gc.get_revision_files(...)` call on the PASS path resolves to AttributeError (caught by the try/except, so degrades) but the fake is otherwise unupdated and unmentioned"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Run the pytest command including tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py and give its `_FakeGerrit.post_vote` a `comments=None` parameter and a `get_revision_files` method.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile MAX_DETAIL_CHARS with adapter.py:145's actual `[:239]` slice (threshold 240) so render_findings_block is genuinely byte-identical, or drop the 'byte-identical' claim.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["adapter.py:145 `detail = f\"{full_detail[:239]}…\" if len(full_detail) > 240 else full_detail` — slice bound is 239, threshold is 240","Plan: 'MAX_DETAIL_CHARS = 240 … detail truncated to MAX_DETAIL_CHARS (ellipsis suffix)' and 'Byte-identical output to today's blocking block for kind \"blocking\"'"],"finding":"The plan claims render_findings_block produces 'byte-identical output to today's blocking block', promoting MAX_DETAIL_CHARS = 240 as 'the exact limit adapter.py:145-152 uses today'. But the current code truncates with full_detail[:239] + ellipsis (slice at 239) triggered when len(full_detail) > 240 — not a slice at 240. Truncating to MAX_DETAIL_CHARS (240) would produce a 240-char body + ellipsis, one char longer than today's output, so the extracted rendering is NOT byte-identical.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcd91483b8e5d6688","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Plan, 'MAX_DETAIL_CHARS = 240' / 'Byte-identical output to today's blocking block'; adapter.py:145","norm_id":"nfe18adbe3d40afa8","priority":0.68,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A blocking finding whose detail exceeds 240 chars: today emits 239 chars + ellipsis; a MAX_DETAIL_CHARS=240 slice emits 240 chars + ellipsis"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State the exact rule: truncate to detail[:MAX_DETAIL_CHARS-1] + ellipsis only when len(detail) > MAX_DETAIL_CHARS, matching adapter.py:145 (slice 239, threshold 240).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State parse_anchor's exact location format contract and reconcile it with the existing `_parse_location` (workflow_ops.py:130 / shim.py:38) — reuse it or explicitly justify the divergent 'None when no usable path' fallback for `path:<non-numeric>` cases.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"parse_anchor(location) — split a free-text location into (path, line|None), tolerating a missing or non-numeric line tail; None when there is no usable path.\"","Existing authoritative parser workflow_ops.py:135-142 / shim.py:42-49 for the SAME field: on a non-numeric line tail it returns `(s, None)` — i.e. the whole string IS a usable path — not None.","Plan's partition rule: \"anchorable only when the parsed path is a key of the revision file map\" — so parse_anchor's path/None decision is load-bearing for AC2/AC4(c,d) inline anchoring.","The plan never states the delimiter/format parse_anchor consumes (e.g. rpartition on ':', line-range / line,col tails), which the existing parser fixes."],"finding":"The plan introduces a new `parse_anchor(location)` decision rule for the finding `location` free-text field without referencing or reconciling with the pre-existing authoritative parser for that same field (`_parse_location` in src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:130 and shim.py:38), which has a materially different fallback and thus a different notion of a 'usable path'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c3a5b938784321f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section: `finding_publish.py` — `parse_anchor(location)`; and `partition_findings`","norm_id":"nd73ecc59837d6286","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A finding whose location is `path:notanumber` or `path:12-15`: existing parser treats `path` as usable; the plan's 'None when no usable path' phrasing leaves the executor free to drop it, changing which findings partition as anchorable (AC4(c)/(d) boundary).","A third divergent location-parsing implementation drifts from the two existing copies."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Reference the existing `_parse_location` as the canonical location-format contract (path via rpartition ':', line-range/col tails tolerated) and either import/reuse it or specify precisely how parse_anchor's anchorability decision differs (e.g. treats `path` with a non-numeric tail as an anchor-less body-only finding), so partition_findings behavior is unambiguous.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"min